    desc: "Haft-sin is the ceremonial sofreh laid for Nowruz, the new year at the vernal equinox, arranged from seven symbolic items each beginning with the letter sin: sabzeh lentil or wheat sprouts for rebirth, samanu wheat pudding for affluence, senjed lotus fruit for love, sir garlic, seeb apples, somaq sumac and serkeh vinegar. Around them gather painted eggs, a mirror and candles, a bowl with goldfish, hyacinth (sonbol), a book of Hafez or the Quran, and coins. Families dress in new clothes, sit before the sofreh at the exact moment of the equinox, exchange gifts and segue into thirteen days of visits, ending with Sizdah Bedar picnics where the sabzeh is cast into running water. The table is the single most recognizable material expression of Persian domestic culture and travels intact through every diaspora kitchen.",
